{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"trust in mobile commerce trust in mobile commerce","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md","fileName":"Trust in Mobile Commerce.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Trust in Mobile Commerce","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-17 09:48\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Mobile Commerce Privacy Behavior]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Mobile Commerce Privacy Behavior","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"trust in mobile commerce trust in mobile commerce","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md","fileName":"Trust in Mobile Commerce.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Trust in Mobile Commerce","heading":"Trust in Mobile Commerce","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Trust in mobile commerce is a user's willingness to rely on a service when its data practices and future behavior cannot be observed completely. Trust can lower perceived privacy risk and make disclosure more likely.\n\nTrust is not a substitute for governance. A user may trust the visible service while being unaware of advertisers, analytics providers, or brokers that receive the information, so transparent boundaries and enforceable duties remain necessary.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Mobile Commerce Privacy Behavior","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Trust in Mobile Commerce.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__non